# Doc Workflow (Shared Atom)

> Applies to: Product-Designer, Frontend-Developer, Backend-Developer, QA-Tester, PM/Lead

---

## 1. Sequential Order

```
PM/Lead: Create Master Doc → Get user approval
    ↓
Product-Designer: Create Product Doc (UX, wireframes)
    ↓
Engineers: Create Engineering Doc (technical specs)
    ↓
QA-Tester: Create QA Doc (test cases)
    ↓
PM/Lead: Create Tasks Doc → Cross-link all docs
    ↓
ALL: Get approvals → Begin implementation
    ↓
Continuous: Update docs with changelog (HH:mm timestamps)
```

---

## 2. Critical Rules

- ❌ **NEVER** create Product/Engineering/QA docs without Master Doc first
- ✅ Master Doc **MUST** be approved before detailed docs
- ✅ Every doc **MUST** have "Related Documents" section with links
- ✅ Every update **MUST** increment version + log in changelog
- ✅ Changelog entries **MUST** include HH:mm timestamps

---

## 3. Doc Responsibility Matrix

| Doc | Creates | Reviews | Approves |
|-----|---------|---------|----------|
| Master Doc | PM/Lead | All roles | User |
| Product Doc | Product-Designer | PM/Lead | User |
| Engineering Doc | Engineers | PM/Lead | User |
| QA Doc | QA-Tester | Engineers | User |
| Tasks Doc | PM/Lead | All roles | User |

---

## 4. Cross-Reference Rules

Every doc's "Related Documents" section **MUST** link:
1. Master Doc (always)
2. Adjacent docs in sequence (Product → Engineering, etc.)
3. GitHub Issue URL
4. PR URL (after implementation)

### Example
```markdown
## Related Documents
- **Master Doc:** `Docs/00-master/push-code-1_master_260407_v1.0.0.md`
- **GitHub Issue:** https://github.com/PersonalProjectJob/Job360/issues/1
```
